  "recordedAt": "2026-09-24",
  "status": "candidate record. Owner approval for this revision is NOT recorded. Production gates have not been run against it. Do not treat it as an approval.",
  "scopeRequested": "One instruction, raised from a screenshot of /ai-gtm: on every page, the left edge of the top bar's wordmark must be the left edge of that page's content. R17 introduced --mm-header-inline so the mark could take each route's own edge, and the body under it was never measured against the result. Four drifts were found and fixed. No page-body redesign, no new commercial offer, no approved copy replaced, and no change to the immutable R3 prototype or its generated adapter.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "Move the shared commercial block onto --mm-header-inline rather than duplicating the route edges into its own stylesheet, because that token already means 'this route's content edge' and the block closes every route it appears on.",
    "Fix .mm-container's auto margin rather than the three blocks that tripped over it: the auto margin and the written-out start margin resolve to the same edge for a container at its own width, and differ only when something narrows the box, which is the bug.",
    "Mirror the R5 surface's --edge into a new .mm-route-leadership class in src/styles/mindmake.css rather than editing src/styles/new-age-leadership-r5.css, which is generated from the approved prototype.",
    "Leave the R3 chapters at their drawn 4.5%, 1.4px inboard of the 4.4% masthead at 1440. That is a composition decision inside the immutable prototype and belongs to the material-review gate, not to a correction pass. It is named in the new gate's exclusions rather than left unrecorded.",
    "Leave the 404 centred. It has no top bar and no content edge; aligning a mark to a centred error card would be a redesign nobody asked for."
  ],
